 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Comparing",
     "texto": [
      "To compare something with another thing, use **N에 비해(서)** (compared with N): 서울**에 비해서** 부산은 한적해요 = compared with Seoul, Busan is quiet.",
      "With a noun that is compared, **에 비해서** goes after the noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Called, known as",
     "texto": [
      "**N(이)라는 N** presents or identifies a name as «called / known as»: 서울**이라는** 도시 = a city called Seoul; 한강**이라는** 강 = a river called Hangang. It is written **-이라는** after a consonant and **-라는** after a vowel.",
      "It does not mean that N is always a proper name: it can also present a designation or an idea."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
